---
import { houstonFacts, monthlyRainfall, houstonClimateSource } from '../data/houston-facts';
---
<section class="section houston-facts" id="houston-facts" aria-labelledby="houstonFactsH">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="houston-facts-heading">
      <h2 id="houstonFactsH">Houston rain.<br>The facts hit home.</h2>
      <p class="lede">From an afternoon downpour to a stalled tropical storm, water needs a place to go. Here&rsquo;s what the local rainfall record—and the cost of flooding—can tell us.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="houston-facts-layout">
      <div class="houston-facts-place">
        <figure class="houston-city-photo">
          <img src="/assets/photos/houston-bayou-1400.webp" srcset="/assets/photos/houston-bayou-640.webp 640w, /assets/photos/houston-bayou-1400.webp 1400w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 45vw" width="1400" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Buffalo Bayou winding through green parkland toward downtown Houston">
          <figcaption><strong>Our city. Our bayous. Our homes.</strong><span>Buffalo Bayou, Houston · <a href="https://unsplash.com/photos/a-city-skyline-with-a-river-running-through-it-VMwl7U2qeNg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Photo: Anvesh Uppunuthula</a></span></figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="houston-rain-chart" aria-labelledby="monthlyRainH">
          <figcaption><h3 id="monthlyRainH">Rain doesn&rsquo;t take a season off.</h3><p>Average rainfall at Houston Intercontinental Airport, by month. Inches, 1991–2020 normals.</p></figcaption>
          <div class="rain-plot" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="rain-chart-scale"><span>6″</span><span>0″</span></div>
            <ol class="rain-bars">
              {monthlyRainfall.map(month => <li><span class="rain-bar-track"><span style={`height:${(month.inches / 6) * 100}%`}></span></span><span>{month.short}</span></li>)}
            </ol>
          </div>
          <details class="rain-data"><summary>See monthly rainfall totals<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chev"/></svg></summary><table><caption>Houston Intercontinental Airport · 1991–2020 normals</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Rainfall (inches)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{monthlyRainfall.map(month => <tr><th scope="row">{month.month}</th><td>{month.inches.toFixed(2)}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></details>
          <a class="rain-chart-source" href={houstonClimateSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source: National Weather Service <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <dl class="houston-facts-list">
        {houstonFacts.map(fact => <div class="houston-fact">
          <dt><strong>{fact.value}</strong><span>{fact.unit}</span></dt>
          <dd><h3>{fact.title}</h3><p>{fact.detail}</p><a href={fact.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{fact.source}<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a></dd>
        </div>)}
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="houston-facts-next">
      <div><h3>Start with the water around your home.</h3><p>Look at roof runoff, low spots, the foundation and the outlet together. A yard drainage system can manage local runoff; street and bayou flooding need a broader plan.</p></div>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/runoff-calculator/">See your roof&rsquo;s runoff <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-arrow"/></svg></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
